/*
 * ll_menu_text.h - the chapter map's FOUR CORNER WORDS as the original
 * engine drew them: the authentic cursive text layer recovered from the
 * QEMU golden-master capture (tools/golden_qemu_run.py): the pixel diff
 * between the captured menu VRAM (idx-plane sha256 ba16421be3c019...) and
 * the clean ANIMACJE/MENU/BACK.PCX index plane IS exactly the engine text -
 * the words WYJSCIE / RESTART / OPCJE / AUTORZY plus the chapter title of
 * whatever was selected at capture time (the title region x15..180 y40..92
 * is NOT included here: the port composites the selected chapter's real
 * LEVELxx.SEQ title instead). Entries are (x, y, palette index) in the
 * 320x200 logical canvas, colored through ll_menu_dac.h like everything
 * else. Extracted 2026-11-15 (PR-37, owner: corner words must be the
 * original stylised text, not the port font). The .SEQ word records
 * (WYJSCIE.SEQ & co) are filled button PLATES, not letters (measured) -
 * these captured bytes are the only record of the cursive corners (the
 * engine's own text font has no asset in any container; PLAN 8b).
 */
